// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 15-function-semantics
// facility: rule.fn.generic-call: a literal argument is checked against its parameter's type unless that type is a number (D-0006); conf.generic-literal-argument-checked
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.type-mismatch (static)
//
// `Option::unwrap(5: u64)` where a `u64` is expected: the expected type
// fixes `T` as `u64`, and the literal is checked against the parameter,
// `Option<u64>`. (A literal argument was exempt from the check whatever
// its parameter's type, so the checker passed this and the C compiler
// failed on what `cobc` made of it; found 2026-10-10.)

import std;

fn main()
{
    u64 x = Option::unwrap(5: u64);
    printf("%v\n", x);
}
